    >>> t = torch.rand(10, 10)
    >>> rfftn = torch.fft.rfftn(t)
    >>> rfftn.size()
    torch.Size([10, 6])

    Compared against the full output from :func:`~torch.fft.fftn`, we have all
    elements up to the Nyquist frequency.

